        -2.98,
        2.28
      ],
      "weight": 1,
      "hypothesis": "Holding the learned state on a coarse grid (e.g. 1/4 res) and decoding per pixel with a tiny implicit MLP cuts the net's cost per eye by several x at equal 96-frame val, which is what Steam Frame resolution (2160^2 per eye) needs."
    },
    {
      "ideaId": "875886c6-a10b-4fa6-83b3-62a68fc1d00b",
      "relativePosition": [
        -2.21,
        3.03
      ],
      "weight": 1,
      "hypothesis": "Predicting where to copy a hole from (infilling vectors toward the background side) instead of a colour beats push-pull on eval96 holes by more than the current +12%, because disocclusions reveal background that sits right next to them."
    },
    {
      "ideaId": "f7c340c1-e7eb-4a58-9448-ebfdeaf551e8",
      "relativePosition": [
        3.25,
        -1.87
      ],
      "weight": 1,
      "hypothesis": "Gating the update by certainty removes most of the all-pixel deficit vs push-pull over 96 frames (-19% -> within -5%) while keeping the +12% on holes. Refuted if all-pixel error stays >10% worse or holes lose their gain.",
      "reflection": "Held, zero-shot: the all-pixel deficit vs push-pull over 96 frames went from -18.9% to -0.7% while holes kept +12.2%."
    }
  ],
